    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serer">Serers</a> believe in a supreme deity, Roog, and address their prayers to the pangool, the ancestral spirits and saints, who are held to carry the prayers of the living to the Divine.</li><li>Each <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serer">Serer</a> family has a totem, the tiim, which is both a prohibition and a guardian: the totem of the Joof family is the antelope, of the Njie the lion, of the Sène the hare.</li><li>At the Xooy ceremony the initiated Saltigue, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serer">Serer</a> high priests and priestesses, foretell the coming year before the community at Fatick, in the first week of June.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serer">Serer</a> spirituality rejects the notion of heaven and hell: a soul accepted by the ancestors may enter Jaaniiw, the place where good souls go, and return to earth through reincarnation, while a rejected soul wanders.</p></aside>
    </section>

